// ast_arena.gopi - Project 2, Phase 2: the self-hosted AST Arena.
//
// A line-for-line-in-spirit (not line-for-line, since Java's AST is a sealed
// hierarchy of immutable records with no arena equivalent) mirror of
// src/main/java/com/gopilang/ast/*.java's node shapes, translated into
// GopiLang's data-oriented shape exactly the way lexer.gopi translated
// Token/TokenType into TokenStream:
//   - Every node - Program, Parameter, FunctionDeclaration, StructDeclaration,
//     every Stmt, every Expr - becomes one row spread across this file's
//     parallel vectors, addressed by a dense num node id (0, 1, 2, ... in
//     allocation order). There is no per-kind struct; one shared column set
//     covers every node kind, exactly as TokenStream's eight columns cover
//     every token kind.
//   - The Parser (selfhost/parser/parser.gopi) is the ONLY writer. Once
//     parsing finishes, nothing further ever calls an arenaSet*/arenaAlloc*
//     function again - the arena is immutable from that point on by
//     convention (GopiLang has no access-control keyword to enforce this
//     mechanically, the same reason BRL's vectors rely on convention, not
//     encapsulation, to keep tokenStreamAppend()/diagnosticBufferAppend()
//     as their sole writers).
//   - No generics, so no single "children: num[]" per node - variable-length
//     child lists (function parameters, block statements, call/construction
//     arguments, struct fields, and Program's own function/struct lists) are
//     stored in ONE shared flat pool vector (childPool), with each node
//     recording (start, count) into that pool - the same "index range into a
//     shared flat store" idiom HashMapTextToNum uses for its three parallel
//     probe-sequence vectors, generalized to variable-length lists instead of
//     fixed-size slots.
//
// Column reuse table (which columns a given node kind actually populates -
// every other column on that row holds its harmless default: -1 for a
// child/list/type/operator slot, 0 for list counts, "" for text, 0.0 for the
// dec literal column - never read, never meaningful, present purely to keep
// every column the same length, exactly as TokenStream's unused literal
// columns already work):
//
//   Program                 : list1 = functions, list2 = structs
//   Parameter                : type0 (+isArray0/structName0), text0 = name
//   FunctionDeclaration      : type0 = return type, text0 = name,
//                              list1 = parameters, child1 = body (Block)
//   StructDeclaration        : text0 = name, list1 = fields (Parameter ids)
//   BlockStatement           : list1 = statements
//   ExpressionStatement      : child1 = expression
//   VariableDeclaration      : type0 = declared type, text0 = name,
//                              child1 = initializer (-1 if none)
//   IfStatement              : child1 = condition, child2 = thenBranch,
//                              child3 = elseBranch (-1 if none)
//   WhileStatement           : child1 = condition, child2 = body
//   ReturnStatement          : child1 = value (-1 if none)
//   PrintStatement           : child1 = value
//   LiteralExpression        : type0.elem = which literal kind (see
//                              primTypeInt/Float/Bool/String below);
//                              child1 = int/bool value, litDec0 = dec value,
//                              text0 = string value (only the one matching
//                              slot is ever populated for a given row)
//   VariableExpression       : text0 = name
//   GroupingExpression       : child1 = inner
//   UnaryExpression          : child1 = operand, operator0 = unary op
//   BinaryExpression         : child1 = left, child2 = right,
//                              operator0 = binary op
//   AssignmentExpression     : text0 = target name, child1 = value
//   FunctionCallExpression   : text0 = calleeName, list1 = arguments
//   NewArrayExpression       : type0.elem = element type, child1 = size
//   ArrayAccessExpression    : child1 = array, child2 = index
//   ArrayLengthExpression    : child1 = array
//   IndexAssignmentExpression: child1 = array, child2 = index, child3 = value
//   NewStructExpression      : text0 = structName, list1 = arguments
//   FieldAccessExpression    : child1 = target, text0 = fieldName
//   FieldAssignmentExpression: child1 = target, child2 = value,
//                              text0 = fieldName
//
// This is a closed, deliberately fixed column set - every node kind above
// already fits within three plain child slots, one list slot (plus
// Program's second list slot), one text slot, one type slot, one dec-literal
// slot, and one operator slot; nothing here anticipates a node kind beyond
// the frozen Java AST's own 4 declaration/program shapes + 7 Stmt + 14 Expr.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// Node kinds - plain zero-argument functions standing in for an enum,
// exactly like lexer.gopi's tokenKindXxx() functions. Numbered in an order
// chosen for this file alone (there is no Java "AST node kind" ordinal to
// cross-reference against, unlike TokenType) - declarations first, then
// statements, then expressions, matching ARCHITECTURE.md's own Stmt/Expr
// grouping.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

num nodeKindProgram() { give 0; }
num nodeKindParameter() { give 1; }
num nodeKindFunctionDeclaration() { give 2; }
num nodeKindStructDeclaration() { give 3; }

num nodeKindBlockStatement() { give 4; }
num nodeKindExpressionStatement() { give 5; }
num nodeKindVariableDeclaration() { give 6; }
num nodeKindIfStatement() { give 7; }
num nodeKindWhileStatement() { give 8; }
num nodeKindReturnStatement() { give 9; }
num nodeKindPrintStatement() { give 10; }

num nodeKindLiteralExpression() { give 11; }
num nodeKindVariableExpression() { give 12; }
num nodeKindGroupingExpression() { give 13; }
num nodeKindUnaryExpression() { give 14; }
num nodeKindBinaryExpression() { give 15; }
num nodeKindAssignmentExpression() { give 16; }
num nodeKindFunctionCallExpression() { give 17; }
num nodeKindNewArrayExpression() { give 18; }
num nodeKindArrayAccessExpression() { give 19; }
num nodeKindArrayLengthExpression() { give 20; }
num nodeKindIndexAssignmentExpression() { give 21; }
num nodeKindNewStructExpression() { give 22; }
num nodeKindFieldAccessExpression() { give 23; }
num nodeKindFieldAssignmentExpression() { give 24; }

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// UnaryOperator / BinaryOperator - mirrors ast.UnaryOperator/BinaryOperator's
// own declared order exactly (ADD, SUBTRACT, MULTIPLY, DIVIDE, MODULO,
// EQUAL, NOT_EQUAL, LESS, GREATER, LESS_EQUAL, GREATER_EQUAL, AND, OR).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

num unaryOpNegate() { give 0; }
num unaryOpNot() { give 1; }

num binaryOpAdd() { give 0; }
num binaryOpSubtract() { give 1; }
num binaryOpMultiply() { give 2; }
num binaryOpDivide() { give 3; }
num binaryOpModulo() { give 4; }
num binaryOpEqual() { give 5; }
num binaryOpNotEqual() { give 6; }
num binaryOpLess() { give 7; }
num binaryOpGreater() { give 8; }
num binaryOpLessEqual() { give 9; }
num binaryOpGreaterEqual() { give 10; }
num binaryOpAnd() { give 11; }
num binaryOpOr() { give 12; }

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// PrimitiveType - mirrors types.PrimitiveType's INT/FLOAT/BOOL/STRING/VOID.
// Also reused, unmodified, as LiteralExpression's own "which literal kind"
// tag (type0.elem) - a literal's type IS always exactly one of these four
// (never VOID), so no separate tag set is needed.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

num primTypeInt() { give 0; }
num primTypeFloat() { give 1; }
num primTypeBool() { give 2; }
num primTypeString() { give 3; }
num primTypeVoid() { give 4; }

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// AstArena - structure-of-arrays, one row per node across every column,
// plus one shared flat pool for every variable-length child list.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

struct AstArena {
    VectorNum kinds;
    VectorNum startLines;
    VectorNum startCols;
    VectorNum endLines;
    VectorNum endCols;
    VectorNum child1;
    VectorNum child2;
    VectorNum child3;
    VectorNum listStart;
    VectorNum listCount;
    VectorNum list2Start;
    VectorNum list2Count;
    VectorText text0;
    VectorNum typeElem;
    VectorNum typeIsArray;
    VectorText typeStructName;
    VectorDec litDec;
    VectorNum operator;
    VectorNum childPool;
}

AstArena arenaCreate() {
    give new AstArena(
            vectorNumCreate(), vectorNumCreate(), vectorNumCreate(), vectorNumCreate(), vectorNumCreate(),
            vectorNumCreate(), vectorNumCreate(), vectorNumCreate(),
            vectorNumCreate(), vectorNumCreate(), vectorNumCreate(), vectorNumCreate(),
            vectorTextCreate(),
            vectorNumCreate(), vectorNumCreate(), vectorTextCreate(),
            vectorDecCreate(),
            vectorNumCreate(),
            vectorNumCreate());
}

num arenaNodeCount(AstArena a) {
    give a.kinds.count;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// Node allocation - the only function that grows the per-node columns
// (childPool grows separately, via arenaChildPoolPush below). Every column
// gets its harmless default; callers fill in only the columns their node
// kind actually uses, via the setters that follow.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

num arenaAlloc(AstArena a, num kind, num startLine, num startCol, num endLine, num endCol) {
    vectorNumPush(a.kinds, kind);
    vectorNumPush(a.startLines, startLine);
    vectorNumPush(a.startCols, startCol);
    vectorNumPush(a.endLines, endLine);
    vectorNumPush(a.endCols, endCol);
    vectorNumPush(a.child1, -1);
    vectorNumPush(a.child2, -1);
    vectorNumPush(a.child3, -1);
    vectorNumPush(a.listStart, 0);
    vectorNumPush(a.listCount, 0);
    vectorNumPush(a.list2Start, 0);
    vectorNumPush(a.list2Count, 0);
    vectorTextPush(a.text0, "");
    vectorNumPush(a.typeElem, -1);
    vectorNumPush(a.typeIsArray, 0);
    vectorTextPush(a.typeStructName, "");
    vectorDecPush(a.litDec, 0.0);
    vectorNumPush(a.operator, -1);
    give a.kinds.count - 1;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// Setters - the Parser calls exactly the ones relevant to the node kind it
// just allocated (see the column-reuse table at the top of this file).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

none arenaSetChild1(AstArena a, num id, num value) { a.child1.items[id] = value; }
none arenaSetChild2(AstArena a, num id, num value) { a.child2.items[id] = value; }
none arenaSetChild3(AstArena a, num id, num value) { a.child3.items[id] = value; }

none arenaSetList1(AstArena a, num id, num start, num count) {
    a.listStart.items[id] = start;
    a.listCount.items[id] = count;
}

none arenaSetList2(AstArena a, num id, num start, num count) {
    a.list2Start.items[id] = start;
    a.list2Count.items[id] = count;
}

none arenaSetText0(AstArena a, num id, text value) { a.text0.items[id] = value; }

none arenaSetType(AstArena a, num id, num elem, num isArray, text structName) {
    a.typeElem.items[id] = elem;
    a.typeIsArray.items[id] = isArray;
    a.typeStructName.items[id] = structName;
}

none arenaSetLitDec(AstArena a, num id, dec value) { a.litDec.items[id] = value; }

none arenaSetOperator(AstArena a, num id, num value) { a.operator.items[id] = value; }

none arenaSetRangeEnd(AstArena a, num id, num endLine, num endCol) {
    a.endLines.items[id] = endLine;
    a.endCols.items[id] = endCol;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// Getters / node lookup - plain column reads by node id. Direct field
// access (a.child1.items[id]) works exactly as well and is used freely
// throughout the Parser too - these exist only where a named call reads
// more clearly than a bare field chain (mirrors BRL's own mix of direct
// field access and small named helpers, e.g. diagnosticBufferSize()).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

num arenaKind(AstArena a, num id) { give a.kinds.items[id]; }
num arenaStartLine(AstArena a, num id) { give a.startLines.items[id]; }
num arenaStartCol(AstArena a, num id) { give a.startCols.items[id]; }
num arenaEndLine(AstArena a, num id) { give a.endLines.items[id]; }
num arenaEndCol(AstArena a, num id) { give a.endCols.items[id]; }
num arenaChild1(AstArena a, num id) { give a.child1.items[id]; }
num arenaChild2(AstArena a, num id) { give a.child2.items[id]; }
num arenaChild3(AstArena a, num id) { give a.child3.items[id]; }
num arenaListStart(AstArena a, num id) { give a.listStart.items[id]; }
num arenaListCount(AstArena a, num id) { give a.listCount.items[id]; }
num arenaList2Start(AstArena a, num id) { give a.list2Start.items[id]; }
num arenaList2Count(AstArena a, num id) { give a.list2Count.items[id]; }
text arenaText0(AstArena a, num id) { give a.text0.items[id]; }
num arenaTypeElem(AstArena a, num id) { give a.typeElem.items[id]; }
num arenaTypeIsArray(AstArena a, num id) { give a.typeIsArray.items[id]; }
text arenaTypeStructName(AstArena a, num id) { give a.typeStructName.items[id]; }
dec arenaLitDec(AstArena a, num id) { give a.litDec.items[id]; }
num arenaOperator(AstArena a, num id) { give a.operator.items[id]; }

// One entry of a node's child list, resolved through (listStart+offset) or
// (list2Start+offset) into the shared pool. offset is 0-based, must be
// < the corresponding listCount/list2Count.
num arenaListAt(AstArena a, num id, num offset) {
    give a.childPool.items[a.listStart.items[id] + offset];
}

num arenaList2At(AstArena a, num id, num offset) {
    give a.childPool.items[a.list2Start.items[id] + offset];
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// Child-list construction. A list is built by pushing every member's node
// id onto the shared childPool, then recording the resulting contiguous
// (start, count) range on the owning node via arenaSetList1/arenaSetList2.
//
// This is safe ONLY as a single contiguous burst with nothing else pushing
// onto childPool in between - NOT by calling arenaChildPoolPush() once per
// member as each is parsed. A member can itself contain a nested construct
// that builds its own list before this list's own loop reaches its next
// element (a block statement containing another block; a call argument that
// is itself a call, e.g. "add(1, add(2, 3))"; a struct-construction argument
// that is itself a struct construction, e.g. "new Box(new Point(1, 2))") -
// that inner list's own pushes would land in between this list's not-yet-
// pushed later members, corrupting the (start, count) window this list
// records. Confirmed by differential testing against Java's Parser on
// exactly these shapes.
//
// Every list-building call site in parser.gopi therefore accumulates member
// ids into its OWN local VectorNum first (parseProgram's functionIds/
// structIds, parseBlock's stmtIds, parseStructDeclaration's fieldIds,
// parseArguments' argIds, parseFunction's inline loop pushing straight into
// the pool - safe there specifically because parameters can never contain a
// nested list of their own), and flushes that local vector into childPool in
// one tight loop only once the full list is known - immediately before
// calling arenaSetList1/arenaSetList2, with no parsing call in between the
// flush and the set.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

num arenaChildPoolBegin(AstArena a) {
    give a.childPool.count;
}

none arenaChildPoolPush(AstArena a, num nodeId) {
    vectorNumPush(a.childPool, nodeId);
}
